  "details": "When we use the print camera to take a photo and print it, the print automatically includes useful info: the photographer’s name, the world name, the world creator’s name, and the date the photo was taken. However, sometimes we need to clear our print inventory to make space for new prints, and once a print is deleted, it’s gone for good.\n\nWe can upload photos, but when we print an uploaded photo, it only shows the date it was printed—not the original date the image was taken, even though that information exists in the metadata. I wish we could print uploaded photos with the same metadata (photographer, world, author, original date taken) just like when printing directly from the print camera.",
